Remarks
The IsolationLevel
values are used by a .NET data provider when performing a transaction.
The IsolationLevel
remains in effect until explicitly changed, but it can be changed at any time. The new value is used at execution time, not parse time. If changed during a transaction, the expected behavior of the server is to apply the new locking level to all statements remaining.
When using OdbcTransaction, if you do not set OdbcTransaction.IsolationLevel or you set it to Unspecified
, the transaction executes according to the isolation level determined by the driver in use.

